---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, isDemoPayment } from '../content/site';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const paymentHref = isDemoPayment ? '#payment-contract' : site.stripeLink;
---
<BaseLayout>
  <main id="main">
    <section id="hero" class="hero section-shell">
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a class="brand" href={base} aria-label="AgentSite home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span> AgentSite</a>
        <div class="nav-links">
          <a class="nav-link" href="#control-plane">Control plane</a>
          <a class="nav-link" href={site.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Contract-driven landing pages for AI agents</p>
          <h1>Let AI agents ship your landing pages without breaking checkout, claims, or brand.</h1>
          <p class="lede">AgentSite turns your offer, brand rules, payment constraints, and QA checks into a machine-readable contract. Coding agents can build, review, deploy, and maintain the site without silently changing approved claims or checkout behavior.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href={site.contractUrl}>View the live contract</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="#workflow">See the agent workflow</a>
          </div>
          <p class="microcopy">This demo uses a safe placeholder checkout link. Live Stripe Payment Links require explicit contract approval.</p>
        </div>
        <aside id="control-plane" class="control-plane" aria-label="AgentSite control plane summary">
          <div class="panel-header">
            <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>AgentSite control plane</span>
          </div>
          <div class="gate-list">
            <div class="gate-row"><span>Contract</span><strong>Approved</strong></div>
            <div class="gate-row"><span>Payment link</span><strong>Locked in demo mode</strong></div>
            <div class="gate-row"><span>Deploy target</span><strong>GitHub Pages · Netlify-ready</strong></div>
            <div class="gate-row"><span>QA gates</span><strong>Contract · Claims · Stripe · Links · Responsive</strong></div>
          </div>
          <div class="trace-card">
            <span class="trace-label">Blocked change</span>
            <p>Attempted checkout swap rejected: live Stripe links require approval.</p>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="problem" class="section-shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The real problem</p>
        <h2>AI can generate a landing page. The hard part is keeping it correct.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="text-card">
        <p>Without an operating contract, agents can invent claims, overwrite payment links, miss SEO basics, ignore mobile issues, or lose context between edits. AgentSite gives the site durable rules before any code changes.</p>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Offer and audience are explicit.</li>
          <li>Claims and brand posture are constrained.</li>
          <li>Payment links are protected.</li>
          <li>Future agents inherit the same rules.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Source of truth</p>
        <h2>The contract is the site’s operating system.</h2>
        <p>Before agents touch code, the contract defines the purpose, deployment target, payment mode, allowed claims, required sections, and QA gates. Agents do not need to infer what matters from scattered docs or chat history.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="code-panel">
        <figcaption>.agent/site.contract.json</figcaption>
<pre><code>requiredSections:
  - hero
  - problem
  - control-plane
  - blocked-change
  - workflow
payment:
  mode: demo
  live links: approval required</code></pre>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="blocked-change" class="section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Guardrails with teeth</p>
      <h2>The contract blocks the edits that should never slip through.</h2>
      <div class="scenario-grid">
        <article class="scenario-card danger">
          <span>Unsafe request</span>
          <p>“Swap checkout to a new payment link and add an unsupported revenue promise.”</p>
        </article>
        <article class="scenario-card locked">
          <span>Contract response</span>
          <p>Blocked: live payment links and unsupported claims require human approval.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="scenario-card allowed">
          <span>Allowed change</span>
          <p>Safe copy and layout improvements can proceed after QA passes.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="workflow" class="section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Subagent operating loop</p>
      <h2>Agents work in parallel, but deploy through gates.</h2>
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Brief → contract</h3><p>The business rules are captured before implementation starts.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Builder</h3><p>A coding subagent implements the page against the contract.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Reviewers</h3><p>Spec, design, payment, SEO, accessibility, and responsive checks run separately.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Deploy</h3><p>Only a contract-compliant artifact ships to the current target.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="payment-contract" class="section-shell payment-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Stripe acceptance without backend risk</p>
        <h2>Payment links are controlled, not improvised.</h2>
        <p>First-stage AgentSites use Stripe Payment Links to avoid secret keys, webhooks, and backend code. Agents can place approved checkout CTAs, but live links are checked against the payment contract. Demo mode intentionally blocks real checkout.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button primary" data-payment-cta="primary" href={paymentHref}>{isDemoPayment ? 'See the payment safety rule' : 'Open approved checkout'}</a>
    </section>

    <section id="qa" class="section-shell qa-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Deploy blockers</p>
        <h2>Every deploy has to pass business-aware checks.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="checks" aria-label="QA gates">
        <li>Required contract fields present</li>
        <li>Contracted sections exist in order</li>
        <li>Forbidden claims absent</li>
        <li>Stripe links allowlisted</li>
        <li>GitHub Pages links stay under base path</li>
        <li>Responsive layouts avoid horizontal overflow</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="cta" class="section-shell final-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">Demo artifact live</p>
      <h2>Start from a landing page agents can understand.</h2>
      <p>This repo demonstrates the AgentSite control-plane pattern: contract, page, payment safety rule, deployment target, and QA gates in one maintainable artifact.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions centered">
        <a class="button primary" href={site.repoUrl}>View source and contract on GitHub</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#control-plane">Review the control plane</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
